description: "guarantees[5]: Explainable Intuition,Reusable Thinking,Predictive Engineering,Cross Domain Transfer,Structured Cognition"
spec:
  id: mental_models
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Cognition
  compiler_stage: Mental Reasoning
  description: "\"Defines the Engineering Mental Model (EMM) framework used by the TOON Dataset Compiler. Mental Models are reusable internal representations that engineers apply to understand, predict, analyze and improve systems. They transform raw knowledge into practical engineering intuition.\""
purpose: Represent engineering intuition as reusable cognitive models.
ekr: Every Engineering Knowledge Record references one or more Mental Models used during reasoning.
examples:
  Example_01:
    Problem: High Latency
    Model: Bottleneck Theory
  Example_02:
    Problem: Deadlock
    Model: Wait-For Graph
  Example_03:
    Problem: Memory Leak
    Model: Object Lifetime
  Example_04:
    Problem: API Scaling
    Model: Queueing Theory
  Example_05:
    Problem: Microservice Failure
    Model: Failure Domains
success: "\"Engineers solve unfamiliar problems by selecting, applying and refining appropriate mental models.\""
future:
  adaptive_model_selection: true
  probabilistic_models: true
  model_composition: true
  self_generated_models: true
  lifelong_model_evolution: true
